body:
@mkinney Could you clarify the contributor procedure for adding the requested screenshots? I can store the four before/after images on the fork’s images-only `pr-screenshots` branch and link them here, leaving the source branch unchanged, as requested.

The current `.claude/skills/issue-claims/references/ownership.md` requires verifying reviewer authority through the base repository’s collaborators API and says to stop if that read fails. GitHub rejects this read for an outside contributor: `403 Must have push access to view repository collaborators.`

What verification should an outside contributor use before recording the evidence writer and publishing the images? A contributor-compatible procedure would resolve this without additional repository permissions. No source changes are proposed.

@mkinney Please recheck the UI evidence finding in comment 7204351563. The PR body now links four native before/after captures for Help/Tips and the start-page tip.

The images are only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch at `e6f6a3078e7bc3990a1d626bb6083f8c388958d5`. The source head remains `7f830a9fce69141dad90752ea4977fa5ef380d32`.

The baseline has no Help/Tips. The after Tips window uses a disclosed temporary debugger state fixture with the unchanged production renderer. This is visual evidence, not successful automated menu-input proof. All four image URLs resolve and match the captured PNGs. Review labels remain unchanged.
